.TH JAILCELL 1 "@@DATE@@" "@@VERSION@@" "Jailcell Manual"
.SH NAME
jailcell \- a secure note-taking and file storage utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jailcell
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICELL_NAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jailcell
is a command-line utility for storing text notes and binary files within an encrypted container. It uses SQLCipher to provide transparent AES-256 encryption for the underlying SQLite database.

If action flags (such as \fB\-\-list\fR, \fB\-\-add\fR, or \fB\-\-show\fR) are present, \fBjailcell\fR executes the specific command and exits immediately. If no action is specified, \fBjailcell\fR starts an interactive Terminal User Interface (TUI).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new
Create a new encrypted cell.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-add
Add a new text note. Requires \fB\-t\fR and \fB\-c\fR.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List all notes and files in the cell.
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-show " id"
Display note content or file metadata for the given ID.
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-title " text"
Set the title for a new note.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-content " text"
Set the content for a new note.
.TP
.BI \-F ", " \-\-file " path"
Import a file from \fIpath\fR into the cell.
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-format " fmt"
Set the output format for listing or showing. Valid formats are \fBtext\fR, \fBjson\fR, and \fBxml\fR. Default is \fBtext\fR.
.TP
.BI \-x ", " \-\-export " id"
Export a file from the cell by its ID. Requires \fB\-o\fR.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " path"
Destination path for exported files.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message.

.SH TUI MODE
Jailcell includes an interactive TUI for managing your cell without manual CLI flags. It uses a modal system inspired by Vim.

.SS Normal Mode
Navigation and action triggers.
.TP
.BR h ", " j ", " k ", " l " / Arrows"
Movement.
.TP
.BR w ", " b
Jump by word.
.TP
.BR { ", " }
Jump by paragraph.
.TP
.BR i ", " I ", " A ", " C
Enter Insert mode (standard Vim behavior).
.TP
.B D
Delete to end of line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open Item Finder/Search.
.TP
.B :
Enter Command mode.

.SS Command Mode
.TP
.B :w
Save changes to the cell.
.TP
.B :q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B :wq
Save and quit.
.TP
.BI :new " title"
Create a new note.
.TP
.BI :rename " name"
Rename the current item.
.TP
.B :delete
Delete the current item.
.TP
.BI :export " path"
Export current item to disk.

.SS Finder Mode (Ctrl+P)
Type to filter items by name. Use \fBj\fR/\fBk\fR to select and \fBEnter\fR to open.

.SH EXAMPLES
Create a new encrypted database:
.IP
.B jailcell -n myvault.db
.PP
Add a note with a title and content:
.IP
.B jailcell -a -t "Meeting" -c "Project plan approved." myvault.db
.PP
Import a binary file:
.IP
.B jailcell -F ./document.pdf myvault.db
.PP
List all entries as JSON:
.IP
.B jailcell -l -f json myvault.db
.PP
Export file with ID 3:
.IP
.B jailcell -x 3 -o ./recovered.pdf myvault.db
.PP
Launch the interactive TUI:
.IP
.B jailcell myvault.db

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR sqlcipher (1)

.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs and find project resources at <https://github.com/mitjafelicijan/jailcell>

.SH ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
